This folder computes the double differential cross section for MEC events at a fixed beam energy and scattering angle
so dsig/dOmega is computed

input_tot_xsec.in is the input card which controls the number of events, beam energy, scattering angle, CC or EM events
as well as whether you want to use a SF or FG, and things about the Delta propagator

The output file is a list of events, the first line is the total cross section, 
the number of trial events(useful for computing unweighting efficiency), and the number of generated events 
Every event contains the 4 vectors of all the particles involved in order:
incoming lepton
outgoing lepton
incoming nucleon 1
outgoing nucleon 1
incoming nucleon 2
outgoing nucleon 2
weight of the event

These can then be fed into an event generator to be cascaded.

If you find that a warning is printed that a weight has been selected which is greater than the max weight
you should unfortunately restart the event generation as this will produced a biased sample
I have only a very simple unweighter implemented, you could change the safety factor
which is the max weight * 1.5 now, you could use a larger safety factor of 2 but the code will be slower
